{"ok": true, "command": "retrieve", "result": {"stopping_reason": "BUDGET_EXHAUSTED_WITH_GAPS", "evidence": [{"id": "DEC-987", "sha256": "df00e1625b2cfcb46f9e733c9dea313d5718070563af52c2acd1e8012e875efa", "path": "docs/DECISION_REGISTER.md", "start_line": 10378, "end_line": 10398, "text": "### DEC-900 \u2014 The AR-9 ruling: RETR-X-02's accepted outcome is the stated gap; W1-42's two accepted reds retired with their entries (P-IS-8 (b))\n- **Status:** ACCEPTED (owner, 2026-10-23, in the chat; recorded and committed by the orchestrator with `Role: orchestrator`, `Task: decision-record`, `Decided-by: owner (chat, 2026-10-23)`) \u00b7 **Under:** DEC-718 item 11, DEC-713, DEC-714, DEC-757, DEC-762, DEC-766, DEC-862 (a), DEC-895, DEC-889 item 16 d \u00b7 **Basis:** lens I's P-IS-8 (`docs/assessment/2026-10/I-SYNTHESIS.md`; I2 F1, I3 F1 and R1). \u00b7 **Changed by:** DEC-906 item 1 (its form): a retirement is a test designer's commit from now on; `c9a08678` stays in history, exempted by exact sha.\n  - Both W1-42 cases read only the frozen Wave 1 exit record.\n  - W2-13's and W2-14's paths cannot reach them.\n  - The kept bundle fails both possible rulings.\n  - W1-21 already asserts the \"stated gap\" outcome on the same scenario.\n- **Decision:**\n  1. **The AR-9 ruling (adoption-readiness item Q-1):** for the cross-section query RETR-X-02, the accepted outcome is **the stated gap**: retrieval states that no named parent expansion exists, as `tests/acceptance/W1-21/` already asserts. This closes DEC-718 item 11's first exception by the owner's ruling.\n  2. **Retired, in one `Role: owner` commit:**\n     - the case `tests/acceptance/W1-42/test_w1_42_exit_report.py::test_retrieval_query_ran_with_bundles_expansions_notes_and_stopping_reason[RETR-X-02]` (its parameter dropped; RETR-A-04 stays);\n     - the function `tests/acceptance/W1-42/test_w1_42_exit_report.py::test_governance_share_is_measured_and_at_most_15_percent_on_each_programme`;\n     - both `accepted_reds` entries (`fixed_by: W2-13`, `fixed_by: W2-14`).\n     The orchestrator prepares the commit and validates it with the pinned ratchet first (DEC-895). **The `accepted_reds` list is then empty.**\n  3. **The requirements live on:**\n     - the parent expansion in W2-13's own acceptance tests;\n     - the measured governance share per programme in W2-14's evidence (DEC-713).\n     The Wave 1 record stays as history.\n- **Changes:** DEC-757's two `accepted_reds` entries (removed); DEC-718 item 11 (the first exception closed by this ruling; the second, the share, by W2-14's evidence); W2-13's and W2-14's cards (no W1-42 case gates their closes).\n- **Where it goes (DEC-851):** this register; RESUME HERE; the prepared owner commit; W2-13's and W2-14's cards' notes. No brief changes.\n- Next free id: DEC-901.\n\n", "chunk_id": "d1e593426db5bb43eb50d0ea", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "DEC-987", "sha256": "d3c4832382f92543cb357cfb5456be598f6c9c172c8e5c8804c1019f6b8fd5ff", "path": "docs/DECISION_REGISTER.md", "start_line": 10382, "end_line": 10392, "text": "  - The kept bundle fails both possible rulings.\n  - W1-21 already asserts the \"stated gap\" outcome on the same scenario.\n- **Decision:**\n  1. **The AR-9 ruling (adoption-readiness item Q-1):** for the cross-section query RETR-X-02, the accepted outcome is **the stated gap**: retrieval states that no named parent expansion exists, as `tests/acceptance/W1-21/` already asserts. This closes DEC-718 item 11's first exception by the owner's ruling.\n  2. **Retired, in one `Role: owner` commit:**\n     - the case `tests/acceptance/W1-42/test_w1_42_exit_report.py::test_retrieval_query_ran_with_bundles_expansions_notes_and_stopping_reason[RETR-X-02]` (its parameter dropped; RETR-A-04 stays);\n     - the function `tests/acceptance/W1-42/test_w1_42_exit_report.py::test_governance_share_is_measured_and_at_most_15_percent_on_each_programme`;\n     - both `accepted_reds` entries (`fixed_by: W2-13`, `fixed_by: W2-14`).\n     The orchestrator prepares the commit and validates it with the pinned ratchet first (DEC-895). **The `accepted_reds` list is then empty.**\n  3. **The requirements live on:**\n     - the parent expansion in W2-13's own acceptance tests;\n", "chunk_id": "8ffc1f33ef6b71149a0de0e9", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "DAEO-zqvn", "sha256": "d75c019fed4f6b41e536f17d698ba45edc9bfb20bea80716b0555a857c648ef6", "path": ".tickets/DAEO-zqvn.md", "start_line": 61, "end_line": 74, "text": "# W2-13 RETR-X-02 and a ranked lexical route (BM25, SQLite FTS5)\n\nCard: `docs/plan/WAVE_2_WBS.md` \u00a72 (W2-13), as approved (DEC-729). The list rows it takes in are in `list_rows` and in `docs/plan/WAVE_2_TRIAGE.md`; a row's state is re-checked against the code when the ticket picks it up (DEC-718).\n\n- **The owner's ruling on RETR-X-02 (Q-1) is made (DEC-900, 2026-10-23):** the accepted outcome is the stated gap.\n- **Allowed paths:** `src/gov/retrieve/**`, `src/gov/retrieval/lexical*`, `src/gov/retrieval/fusion*`, `src/gov/rebuild/lexical*`, `tests/unit/retrieve/**`, `tests/unit/retrieval/**`.\n- **KPIs, success:**\n  - **The ranked lexical route.** The lexical index is an SQLite FTS5 table over the same parents and spans as today, built by `gov rebuild` (and, after W2-06, by the commit-time re-index). A plain-word question returns hits ranked by BM25, with field weights for id, title and body. An exact identifier still ranks first: the exact-match route is kept as a boost, not replaced [DEC-725, W2-M102, W2-L233, W2-M292, W2-M072, W2-M100].\n  - The fusion receives a ranked lexical list beside the semantic one, so that lexical, semantic and the reranker each contribute. The dev queryset's lexical-only hit@5 is recorded in the ticket's evidence [DEC-725].\n  - Lexical search returns \"unavailable\" instead of raising [W2-M071]. Retrieval latency stays within the retrieve budget on the dev tiers.\n  - A question about an id that exists nowhere stops with a named reason and no unrelated items: the stated gap, as the owner ruled for RETR-X-02 (DEC-900, AR-9), and as W1-21 asserts; W1-42's RETR-X-02 case is retired, so this ticket's own acceptance tests hold the requirement [AR-9, W2-M296, DEC-900].\n- **KPIs, failure:**\n  - RETR-A-04's bundle is unchanged (citations, three parent expansions, stopping reason).\n  - The secrets filter applies to the FTS5 table as to the old index: a planted canary is never indexed.\n", "chunk_id": "e7e6489d12e7a04631c57639", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "59069b24dfd54cf9e7b61562", "sha256": "0f3c82501a2bf0adc549c4544ab62380f207ab92d4c00f7976dc6243f09d7a6b", "path": "docs/plan/wave-1-exit/EXIT-REPORT.md", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 40, "text": "## Adoption-readiness block (opens Wave 2)\n\nThe owner's intended exit names four exceptions, accepted, each a line here with what it is, the evidence that shows it and what would close it; the a-dev clone's three reds have a line each. Together they open Wave 2 and must pass before any pilot adoption (DEC-714); the same block stands in the orchestrator's running record (`governance/project/bootstrap.md`, its Wave 2 list). Before all of them comes the FIRST item of the Wave 2 list (DEC-712), the last line below. None of these lines changes a verdict of \"Exit criteria\".\n\n- **ARGUS's incomplete cycle (b-dev adopted to A2):** ARGUS ran every step from discovery to the implementation (65 of 65 cases green) and stops at the close: `gov close ARGUS-im01` refused with `CONTEXT_FAILED` (exit 3), because b-dev is adopted to A2 only and its store does not hold the ticket's source REQ-004; no CI and no merge exist, eight check families of b-dev are red at `fc28272` from its legacy records, and b-dev's canaries were not run. Evidence: `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/close-ARGUS-im01-store-stale.json`, `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/close-ARGUS-im01-refused.json`, `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/gov-check-b-dev.json`, `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/b-dev-history.txt`; the section \"Programme ARGUS\". Closes when ARGUS's feature runs the full cycle to a clean close, CI and merge: b-dev adopted far enough that its store holds the ticket's sources, one `gov close` of ARGUS's implementation ticket with exit 0, no disposition and no exception, its `gov ci` and its merge, each kept as an answer under the evidence folder, so that the ARGUS rows close, CI and merge read `done`.\n- **a-dev's red, context reproducibility (ORION-gp01):** `gov check` in a-dev at `127227c`, after a full rebuild with embeddings, is red on context reproducibility with 1 finding: two computations of ORION-gp01's context give two hashes (`d2d9f759...` and `5fdcf8ab...`), the same two in runs 6, 7 and 8; on run 8's stale store the same check was green. Run 6's reading of the cause (the first computation in a process orders supplementary items that rank next to each other differently) was not measured again. Evidence: `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/gov-check-a-dev-run8.json`, `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/gov-check-a-dev-run8-stale-store.json`, `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/gov-check-a-dev-run7-ci-head.json`, `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/ci-a-dev-run7-red-findings.json`. What the finding needs: the product's, a context that gives the same items in the same order on every computation, with the cause measured. Closes when `gov check` in a-dev, on a store freshly rebuilt with embeddings, is green on context reproducibility with ORION-gp01 named by no finding, and `gov ci checks G1 G2` no longer names context-reproducibility.\n- **a-dev's red, concurrency/claims (3 findings):** all three `TICKET_MISSING_FIELD` on ade-ke2y, the repair ticket the refused second `gov close ORION-im01` wrote: it lacks role, allowed_paths and kpis. Its close with the ticket tool (DEC-708) did not clear them: the check judges a closed ticket's fields too. Evidence: `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/gov-check-a-dev-run8.json`, `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/ci-a-dev-run7-red-findings.json`. What the findings need: ade-ke2y's three fields, as ade-5rcs got them in run 7 (in the clone, a new commit, which DEC-708's \"history is not rewritten\" allows; ordering it is the owner's); for the product, `gov close` writing a repair ticket with role, allowed paths and KPIs (the residual of DEC-674). Closes when `gov check` in a-dev is green on concurrency/claims.\n- **a-dev's red, schema/invariants (4 findings):** three `SCHEMA_MISSING_FIELD` on ade-ke2y (the same three fields: kpis, role, allowed_paths) and one `SCHEMA_UNKNOWN_TYPE` on ORION-im02's close record, which `gov close` wrote with the record type `close` that the schemas of the same installation do not know. Evidence: `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/gov-check-a-dev-run8.json`, `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/ci-a-dev-run7-red-findings.json`. What the findings need: the first three clear with the claims line's edit of ade-ke2y; the fourth is the product's, the schemas knowing the record type the close writes (or the close writing one they know), so that the first `gov check` after a clean close is not red on it. Closes when `gov check` in a-dev is green on schema/invariants.\n- **RETR-X-02 (no parent expansion):** asked once in each of runs 6 and 7, `gov retrieve \"What does DEC-9999 decide?\" --id DEC-9999 --radius 1` returns 2 batches, 20 items cited by id and hash, the missing id as a stated gap and a valid bundle, but no parent expansion; criterion 2 asks named parent expansions, and W1-42's case for RETR-X-02 is red on \"no named parent expansion\". Evidence: `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/RETR-X-02.json`, beside `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/RETR-A-04.json` (three named expansions); the section \"Retrieval\". Closes on a kept bundle of RETR-X-02 with at least one parent expansion that names its parent, or on the owner's ruling on whether a question about an id that exists nowhere has to show a parent expansion.\n- **ARGUS's governance share (missing):** no share is measured for ARGUS: no ticket of b-dev has a close record (its one `gov close` refused), and on two of its tickets the session-start and hook parts are of an attachment type no specimen shows; its estimated shares are 1.29 % to 2.50 %. The one measured total of the exit run is ORION-im02's, 4.49 %; criterion 4 asks a share of each programme, and ORION's is not measured per programme either (see \"Governance share\"); DEC-714 names ARGUS's as the exception. Evidence: the section \"Governance share\", `docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/telemetry-ORION-im02.json`. Closes on a measured share of at most 15 % on ARGUS's run: the counter's measure after a clean close of ARGUS's tickets, every part measured, kept as the counter's answer and entered for ARGUS in governance-share.json.\n- **FIRST on the Wave 2 list, before any pilot adoption (DEC-712): the hook's git environment.** In a linked worktree the pre-commit hook wrote two foreign commits onto this branch (DEC-710, DEC-711); the cause read from the code, not run: `src/gov/retrieval/retrieve_check.py` runs `git -C <temporary clone> add -A` and `commit` with the `GIT_*` variables the hook inherits. The item: checks and tests that run git clear the inherited `GIT_*` variables; a sweep of every check, test helper and command that runs git in another folder; `lefthook install` and `uninstall` re-sorting `.claude/settings.json`, so that installing the hooks never leaves adapter-portability red. Evidence: DEC-710 to DEC-712 in `docs/DECISION_REGISTER.md`, the Wave 2 list in `governance/project/bootstrap.md`. Closes when a hooked commit in a linked worktree leaves its branch and index as the commit made them, the sweep is kept, and the hooks install with adapter-portability green.\n\n", "chunk_id": "59069b24dfd54cf9e7b61562", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "b9bed5e653231cb9768d439f", "sha256": "b0ddaa963a8f6cc51c5c1ae392ebe05e7dcf76784d7908a2e447ca406d802605", "path": "docs/contract/contract.yaml", "start_line": 1046, "end_line": 1091, "text": "    from the fixed list; a batch-size limit is never reported as completeness.\n  wave: W1\n  wave_note: DEC-080\n  provider:\n  - W1-21\n  - W1-36\n  sources:\n  - OWNER-DIRECTION-BR-0005 (full)\n  - OWNER-DIRECTION-BR-0006 \u00a72, \u00a73\n  - DEC-030, DEC-033, DEC-034, DEC-035\n  - DEC-080\n  scenarios:\n    dev:\n    - RETR-A-04\n    - RETR-X-02\n    qual:\n    - RETR-A-Q01\n    - RETR-A-Q02\n    - RETR-A-Q03\n    - RETR-A-Q04\n    - RETR-X-Q02\n    - RETR-X-Q05\n  disposition:\n    class: KEPT\n  covers:\n  - id: CAP-16.a\n    item: Batches with continuation; batch size never a completeness limit\n    source: DEC-030; DEC-080; OWNER-DIRECTION-BR-0005\n    wave: W1\n    provider:\n    - W1-21\n  - id: CAP-16.b\n    item: Parallel facet retrieval \u2192 merge/filter \u2192 unresolved dependencies \u2192 sequential follow-up \u2192 bounded compilation\n    source: DEC-030; OWNER-DIRECTION-BR-0006 \u00a72, \u00a73\n    wave: W1\n    provider:\n    - W1-36\n    - W1-21\n  - id: CAP-16.c\n    item: Radius-scaled rounds (placeholders tuned from telemetry)\n    source: DEC-035\n    wave: W1\n    provider:\n    - W1-21\n- id: CAP-17\n  title: Incremental indexing and freshness\n", "chunk_id": "b9bed5e653231cb9768d439f", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "DEC-987", "sha256": "54187777180bbfa972c7ed9aa47fd108a92ba82416287b0f54b8706caa6ff622", "path": "docs/DECISION_REGISTER.md", "start_line": 11607, "end_line": 11628, "text": "### DEC-943 \u2014 Brief gaps in every lead's return, fixed the same week; the orchestrator's own drift measured (standing)\n- **Status:** ACCEPTED (owner, 2026-10-29, in the chat; recorded and committed by the orchestrator with `Role: orchestrator`, `Task: decision-record`, `Decided-by: owner (chat, 2026-10-29)`; standing) \u00b7 **Under:** DEC-824, DEC-793, DEC-836, DEC-930, DEC-938, DEC-941, CAP-33\n- **Decision:**\n  1. **Brief gaps.** Every lead's return gains a \"brief gaps\" section: what it had to discover, look up or ask that its brief, ticket or skills did not tell it, with the time it cost.\n     - The orchestrator collects them and fixes the common brief, the brief builder or the kernel skills the same week.\n     - The daily document reports how many gaps were found and how many fixed.\n     - W2-79's tests check that each fixed gap stays fixed.\n  2. **The orchestrator's drift.** Once W2-61's baseline and the first memory fixes (W2-55, W2-04) land, the orchestrator uses `gov context` at every resume and before every decision that touches a standing rule. It counts, weekly, every time it acted against a standing decision; that count is the measure of its own drift.\n- **How it is applied:**\n  - **The lead brief** (`governance/project/briefs/LEAD-w2-common.md`, Return): a `brief_gaps:` section right after the twelve fields, every status. Each line names what was missing, where it belonged (common brief, the ticket's part, the ticket file, a skill, a tool) and the minutes it cost. Briefs built from 2026-10-29 17:20 carry it.\n  - **The register of gaps:** `governance/project/orchestration/brief-gaps.md`, one row per gap: the date, the ticket, the gap, its home, the minutes, and the fixing commit or \"open\".\n  - **Fixing:**\n    - a gap in the common brief or the builder is fixed by the orchestrator, recorded under this decision;\n    - a gap in a kernel skill goes through CIT-P the same week (CAP-33: no kernel change without evidence, review and owner approval), so \"fixed\" there means proposed with its evidence, then promoted.\n  - **W2-79's ticket** gains a KPI: one case per fixed gap in the common brief or the builder, showing that a built brief still carries the fix.\n  - **Drift:**\n    - the trigger is W2-61's baseline record plus W2-55's and W2-04's closes;\n    - from then, the prompt \u00a71 adds `gov context` to every resume and before every decision touching a standing rule;\n    - the weekly numbers (DEC-930) gain a fifth: acts against a standing decision, each named with the decision and how it was found (the orchestrator's own count, the owner's correction, an auditor);\n    - until the trigger, the count is kept by hand from the owner's corrections and the slips list.\n- **Where it goes (DEC-851):** this register; `LEAD-w2-common.md` (Return); the prompt \u00a71 (item 5, `gov context` once the trigger is met) and \u00a77 (the daily document's lines), v3.40; `brief-gaps.md`; W2-79's ticket; RESUME HERE.\n\n", "chunk_id": "75d172976e3286806171905b", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "DEC-987", "sha256": "48b2c99d2ad857561fe6c907d9b05fc85b62c82ce5f07283518384cde0ad436b", "path": "docs/DECISION_REGISTER.md", "start_line": 12091, "end_line": 12103, "text": "### DEC-965 \u2014 W2-90's run 1: merged with 7 named reds; its parameter splits, the 236th case and a resume for the 14 ids ACT 1 dropped (delegated)\n- **Status:** ACCEPTED (orchestrator, delegated under DEC-936 item 2.5: P2s, reversible, the orchestrator's recommendation and the lead's agree, confidence medium to high, nothing in the Charter, the master rules or the Contract's scope, the guard not weakened; for the owner to overturn) \u00b7 **Under:** DEC-957 (ACT 1 option (a)), DEC-953 item 2, DEC-906 \u00b7 **Basis:** W2-90's run-1 return (`log/W2-90-A5-run1.json`, 2026-10-31 01:12)\n- **Decision:**\n  1. **Merged now** (`21eac66b`): 228 of the 235 cases judge the kernel's wiring and pass on both heads; the 7 that cannot move without lowering stay red, named: W1-05's two orchestrator-asks cases and W1-46's research `npm-install` case (the template denies installs, P1-A), and four W2-59 cases (the template's hook line has no pinned interpreter, P1-B). Both P1s go to the owner (`packages/P-W2-90-1.md`).\n  2. **P2-C (a):** the test designer's splits of two mixed functions by parameter, and W1-49's two containment parameters moved to a new function, are accepted: every id is kept or mapped, the count unchanged.\n  3. **P2-D (a):** the 236th ACT-1 red (`W1-05::test_the_hooks_stay_wired_in_every_later_commit`), revised the same way in a file already in scope, is accepted into W2-90.\n  4. **P2-E (a):** the 14 parametrized ids ACT 1 removed without a red (W2-59's 10 post-tool ids, W2-65's 4) and W2-59's empty-parameter skip are moved to the template's post-tool lines by a test designer in W2-90's next round, with the owner's answers to P1-A and P1-B.\n- **Where it goes (DEC-851):** this register; W2-90's ticket and its run-2 brief; RESUME HERE.\n\n| Version | Date | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.348 | 2026-10-31 | Delegated (orchestrator, DEC-936 item 2.5): DEC-965 (W2-90 merged with 7 named reds; P2-C, P2-D, P2-E (a)). Next free id: DEC-966. |\n\n", "chunk_id": "81f49e8486a2e97ac3031ce6", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "DEC-987", "sha256": "0627861b6d6115a4c2246e57f5839ce01064fa895ab840f94384454fd9740d0f", "path": "docs/DECISION_REGISTER.md", "start_line": 10896, "end_line": 10918, "text": "### DEC-921 \u2014 The two unpushed W2-59 and W2-65 merges are replaced by one merge of `w2/W2-65`, under three conditions; W2-73 for W1-03's fixture\n- **Status:** ACCEPTED (owner, 2026-10-25, in the chat; recorded and committed by the orchestrator with `Role: orchestrator`, `Task: decision-record`, `Decided-by: owner (chat, 2026-10-25)`) \u00b7 **Under:** DEC-884, DEC-918, DEC-410, DEC-750, DEC-754 \u00b7 **Basis:** package P-W2-65-M1 (`governance/project/orchestration/packages/P-W2-65-M1.md`): merging `w2/W2-59` (`e77ffb54`) and then `w2/W2-65` (`45a6dfd5`) gave the second merge two merge bases, which containment reads fail closed, so W2-65's close would be refused; one merge of `w2/W2-65` (which holds W2-59) has one merge base and the same tree.\n- **Decision:**\n  1. **Yes to (a)**, with three conditions:\n     - before the reset, confirm that no dropped commit is on origin (never force-push; if any is pushed, stop and bring a package);\n     - keep a backup ref of the head first, not deleted until the re-pin has passed its smoke test;\n     - after the single merge, confirm the tree is `30442e9f` and that containment, the trailer gate and W1-01 all judge it clean.\n  2. **Then** create W2-73 (LITE) for W1-03's fixture, and send the re-pin ACT package.\n- **Done (2026-10-25):**\n  - **Origin:** after a fetch, `origin/w2/integrate` was at `18ad2382`, behind `4a57bf6b`; `git branch -r --contains` found neither `e77ffb54` nor `45a6dfd5`.\n  - **Backup ref:** `w2/integrate-before-reset-2026-10-24` at `45a6dfd5`.\n  - **Reset and merge:** reset to `4a57bf6b`, then one merge `6a4696eb` (Task: DAEO-e82f, both tickets named); tree `30442e9f`, equal to git's merge-tree, one merge base (`fa53ba34`).\n  - **Containment:** no finding over the 105 commits of W2-65, W2-59, W2-72 and W2-66, nor in any pending ticket's merges.\n  - **Trailer gate:** nothing lacking for those four tickets.\n  - **W1-01:** the history and integration-merges cases pass (37 passed, 3 skipped).\n- **Changes:** DEC-884 item 3 (the two tickets merge in one merge of the stacked branch).\n- **Where it goes (DEC-851):** this register; package P-W2-65-M1 (committed with this record); RESUME HERE; the re-pin ACT package.\n- Next free id: DEC-922.\n\n| Version | Date | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.307 | 2026-10-25 | Owner (recorded by the orchestrator, DEC-861): DEC-921 (P-W2-65-M1 (a) under three conditions: nothing dropped was on origin; backup ref `w2/integrate-before-reset-2026-10-24` kept until the re-pin's smoke test; one merge `6a4696eb` of `w2/W2-65`, tree `30442e9f`, judged clean by containment, the trailer gate and W1-01; then W2-73 for W1-03's fixture and the re-pin ACT). Next free id: DEC-922. |\n\n", "chunk_id": "3e277608d1e21fb46ff44ded", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "DEC-987", "sha256": "ddf5f9c399e6d24e927a3b4f639db91e6b1cd4ad0bcdadc83ce3b178f2ca6b1f", "path": "docs/DECISION_REGISTER.md", "start_line": 11279, "end_line": 11286, "text": "- **Where it goes (DEC-851):** this registe